From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] t41: define cpu_has_mxuv3 for the mainline kernel

The recovered TMO selector tests the vendor cpu_has_mxuv3 feature flag,
which the mainline 7.x kernel does not provide, so the T41 module does
not compile.  The T41 is XBurst2-MXU3.1 and this module only builds for
the T41, so expose the flag as always set in the compat header.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/driver/t41/tx_isp_t41_kernel_compat.h
+++ b/driver/t41/tx_isp_t41_kernel_compat.h
@@ -41,6 +41,13 @@
 #define PDE_DATA(inode) pde_data(inode)
 #endif
 
+/* The T41 is XBurst2-MXU3.1.  The mainline kernel does not expose the
+ * vendor's cpu_has_mxuv3 feature flag, and this module only builds for
+ * the T41, so the SIMD path is always available here. */
+#ifndef cpu_has_mxuv3
+#define cpu_has_mxuv3 1
+#endif
+
 struct proc_dir_entry *jz_proc_mkdir(const char *name, ...);
 
 /* set_fs()/KERNEL_DS are gone; the V4L2 bridge still spells them out. */
